README for tests of the MEX interace for the AL

1. Running the tests

The tests use the testing framework from MATLAB. The main file is the imas_test.m file and the tests can be run b the following command (from the MATLAB prompt):

>> results = runtests('imas_test')

2. Tests breakdown

For each IDS, four tests are run. They rely on random (but repeatable) generation of IDSs, see the dedicated section for more details. The four tests are:
  - PUT+GET recovers the full IDS
  - PUT+GET_SLICE recovers the sliced IDS
  - PUT_NON_TIMED+PUT_SLICE+GET recovers the sliced IDS
  - PUT_NON_TIMED+PUT_SLICE+GET_SLICE recovers the sliced IDS
A comparator function has been implemented to test that the correct value has been recovered

NB: For the testing framework to work we need each test function to be explicitely defined in the main file, hence it was necessary to generate those using XSLT.

3. Generating IDSs

The random generation of IDSs has been adapted from the one developed for the MATLAB interface (new lowlevel). Each IDS can be generated with several slices or a single time slice. The single time slice is the same as the first time slice when several are generated.

NB: So far IDSs with homogeneous time base only can be generated